Platform marks for the Export page's preset cards
=================================================

Source: Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), simple-icons@13.21.0 from
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/simple-icons@13.21.0/icons/<slug>.svg

The Simple Icons SVG data is released under CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication). The brand
marks themselves are trademarks of their respective owners (YouTube and YouTube Shorts:
Google LLC; Instagram and Facebook: Meta Platforms, Inc.; TikTok: ByteDance Ltd.; X: X Corp.;
Vimeo: Vimeo.com, Inc.; Twitch: Twitch Interactive, Inc.). Simple Editor uses them only to
identify the platform an export preset is made for; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by
any of them. Follow each owner's brand guidelines if you reuse them.

Files
-----
<slug>.svg   the original Simple Icons path (24 x 24 viewBox), unchanged
<slug>.png   64 x 64 white glyph on a transparent background, embedded in the exe by
             src/ui/brand_icons.rs and tinted with the brand colour when painted

Slugs: youtube, youtubeshorts, tiktok, instagram, x, facebook, vimeo, twitch

The PNGs are made by scripts/brand-icons.sh (headless Edge renders each SVG black on white at
64 px, ffmpeg turns that into a white-on-alpha mask), so the app needs no SVG renderer. Run it
again after replacing an SVG. This folder is not part of the online icon library (that only
reads the .svg files directly in library/icons).
